; `blade_base` and `blade_tip` are deliberately NOT wired here any more. They used to
; point at two marker nodes inside the inline sword; the markers now arrive with
; whatever is equipped, so Player rebinds them through the Loadout on every swap. A
; weapon with no markers (the bow, the shield) leaves them null and the ribbon simply
; never draws, which is what SwordTrail._physics_process already does with a null.
[node name="SwordTrail" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="."]
cast_shadow = 0
material_override = SubResource("StandardMaterial3D_trail")
script = ExtResource("18_trail")
width_curve = SubResource("Curve_trail_width")

; The charge tell's ground ring. Sits marginally higher than the spin's so the two
; can never z-fight if a charge is somehow live across a spin, and a child of the
; Player rather than of Rig so it does not inherit the spin's two revolutions.
